# "Whenever YOU sacrifice another permanent": Bot2 sacrificing its own Lotus Petal, as Bot1's Peddlers watches, gives it nothing; nor
# does a permanent of Bot1's that is destroyed (Disenchant on its Mox) rather than sacrificed. Bot1's own Lotus Petal, sacrificed for
# mana, gives exactly one counter, so the Peddlers is 3/3 and not the 2/2 it was.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Pirate Peddlers
Lotus Petal
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Lotus Petal
Disenchant
Plains x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pirate Peddlers.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: White)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Pirate Peddlers.Power = 2
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Disenchant.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Pirate Peddlers.Power = 2
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: Black)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Pirate Peddlers.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Pirate Peddlers.Power = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Lotus Petal; Mox Pearl
